---
import Callout from "../atoms/Callout.astro";
import Link from "../atoms/Link.astro";
---

<section
  class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-md p-4 lg:mt-25 lg:grid lg:max-w-360 lg:grid-cols-7 lg:gap-x-8 lg:px-15 lg:py-6"
>
  <h2
    class="font-display text-primary text-xl font-bold lg:col-span-2 lg:text-4xl"
    style="line-height: 92%"
  >
    Q&A
  </h2>

  <dl class="mt-4 text-pretty lg:col-span-4 lg:mt-2.25 lg:text-2xl">
    <dt>
      1. What is the <abbr>NPLB</abbr> Fellowship and how is it connected to the Biotech
      Unveiled Course?
    </dt>
    <dd>
      The <abbr>NPLB</abbr> Fellowship is a logical continuation of the Biotech Unveiled
      Course. Both were launched by <abbr>RA</abbr> Capital and <abbr>NPLB</abbr
      > with a mission to prepare future biotech leaders. The Biotech Unveiled course
      is the first step, and its completion is required to apply for the Fellowship.
      As a Fellow, you will join the cohort of bright, like-minded individuals from
      all over the world, gain access to the advanced biotech materials, participate
      in live sessions with leaders of the biotech industry, get mentorship from them,
      and work on group projects. Invited guests include key investors, big pharma
      leaders, health policymakers from the <abbr>UK</abbr>, Europe and the <abbr
        >US</abbr
      >.
    </dd>

    <dt>2. How long does it take to finish the Course?</dt>
    <dd>It takes around 1–2 weeks to complete at a relaxed pace.</dd>

    <dt>3. Which markets does this course focus on?</dt>
    <dd>
      Practice and examples in this course are focused mainly on <abbr>US</abbr
      > market. However, it will be useful for learners looking to access
      European market as well. This choice is intentional: Biotech industry is
      global, and currently the <abbr>US</abbr> shapes much of the global biotech
      playbook. Market mechanics — drug development, investment, pricing debates,
      company strategies, and what eventually reaches patients — are similar in the <abbr
        >US</abbr
      >
      and Europe. The key question — How do we make medicines affordable while keeping
      them worth developing? — matters to patients everywhere.
    </dd>

    <dt>4. Who are you and why are you promoting this course?</dt>
    <dd>
      We are current <abbr>NPLB</abbr> Fellows with diverse backgrounds who firmly
      believe that the <abbr>UK</abbr> has an untapped potential for bringing more
      biotech innovations to patients' bedsides. For us the Biotech Unveiled Course
      and <abbr>NPLB</abbr> Fellowship became a mind-changing experience — and we would
      like to bring this experience to our peers across <abbr>UK</abbr> academia and
      industry. We are certain that, equipped with the knowledge the Course and the Fellowship
      provide, you will be able to bring your ideas to life with a much greater chance
      of success.
    </dd>

    <dt>5. I am still uncertain or have questions — who can I talk to?</dt>
    <dd>
      You can contact any of us through emails listed in <Link href="#contacts"
        >the “Contacts” section</Link
      >
      — we are always happy to chat and answer any questions you may have!
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <Callout class="mt-9 lg:col-span-5 lg:col-start-2 lg:mt-38"
    >Biotech is not just about discovering medicines. It is about building
    systems where medicines can reach people
  </Callout>
</section>

<style>
  @reference '../../styles/global.css';

  dt {
    @apply text-primary font-semibold;
    line-height: 144%;
  }

  dt:not(:first-of-type) {
    @apply mt-6 lg:mt-9;
  }

  dd {
    line-height: 144%;
  }
</style>
